  "verdict": {
    "outcome": "O4",
    "direction": "negligible",
    "magnitude": "minor",
    "time_horizon": "long-term",
    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "This rail reform policy is mainly about restructuring how trains are run, not about pay or employment rights for workers. The evidence provided says little about effects on workers' wages or job security, so the impact on good work and fair pay is at most minor and unclear.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether integrating fragmented rail operators under GBR improves or worsens frontline rail workers' pay, security, and conditions depends on the employment model chosen \u2014 which the evidence does not address.",
